Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":": counts pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" quickly (K₂₅ has 25²³). A dense Cholesky factorization of the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Laplacian with one vertex removed, its pivots multiplied with the binary exponent kept apart,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so the result overflows only past "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"’s range, to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".infinity"},{"type":"text","text":". When every weight is an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"integer (unweighted included) a result below 2⁵³ is rounded to the nearest integer, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"then exact; nearer to 2⁵³ and above, it is within a relative 10⁻¹² or so, not exact. O(n³) time,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"n² "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/numberofspanningtrees()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/numberOfSpanningTrees()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory":{"abstract":[],"title":"SpectralGraphTheory","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory"},"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols":{"role":"collection","abstract":[],"type":"topic","title":"GraphProtocols","url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphpr